      "drawing_body_index": 91,
      "caption_body_index": 92,
      "caption": "Fig. S2. Rater annotations and prediction variability in one five-rater evaluation case, selected nearest the median localization error among 14 eligible images before visual review. (A) The five raters' landmark coordinates and the reference obtained by averaging each landmark's coordinates across raters. (B) The same reference and the mean landmark coordinates across 50 dropout predictions. The reference is not anatomical truth; segments join angle-defining landmarks. (C–E) P4 offsets from the mean across dropout predictions (+). Panels show the average covariance predicted within each pass after centering the component means (C), covariance of the 50 predicted means across passes (denominator 50; D), and total covariance with 1,024 illustration-only mixture samples (E). All ellipses have Mahalanobis radius one, not confidence-interval coverage. Panels A and B share coordinate bounds; panels C–E share offset bounds; all axes have equal pixel scales. These P4 distributions describe one landmark and do not validate the full joint distribution.",
