      "caption": "Fig. S4. Angle error among retained images in 242 internal-evaluation images. (A, B) Alpha/beta MAE after retaining images with the lowest scores: total angular SD, SD from variation between dropout predictions, SD from uncertainty predicted within each dropout pass, or average landmark spread. Each curve contains every retained count from 121 to 242. The expected MAE under random retention equals the all-image MAE; it is not estimated from one random subsample. The oracle ranks images by their observed reference errors and is unavailable in prospective selection (shown only as a retrospective lower bound). Whiskers on Total and Landmark spread show 95% image-bootstrap CIs from 10,000 reranked resamples at 121, 194, and 242 images (50.0%, 80.2%, and 100%). All methods use identical predictions and reference errors. Coincident full-retention estimates represent the same images.",
